},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Robert Simms","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10842","person_slug":"robert-simms","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sam Dastyari","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10819","person_slug":"sam-dastyari","vote":"no"},{"name":"Sarah Hanson-Young","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10711","person_slug":"sarah-hanson-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sean Edwards","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10756","person_slug":"sean-edwards","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Conroy","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10142","person_slug":"stephen-conroy","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Lines","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10782","person_slug":"sue-lines","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zed Seselja","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10822","person_slug":"zed-seselja","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Business — Rearrangement","noes":22,"question":"Penny Wong I seek leave to move a motion adjourning the two items of business—adjourning the Tax Laws Amendment (Combating Multinational Tax Avoidance) Bill 2015 to a later hour. Leave not granted. I move: That so much of standing orders be suspended as would prevent me moving a motion adjourning these items to a later hour of the day. Mitch Fifield Mr Acting Deputy President, I rise on a point of order. The Senate has already determined that the motion which I was seeking to move and have indeed moved would be moved immediately and determined without amendment or debate. There is currently a question before the chair. Senator Wong sought leave to suspend standing orders to move an amendment to the motion that I had moved. The Senate determined that that should not happen. Senator Wong is now seeking to bring an entirely different question before the chamber. She is not seeking to amend my motion, so the motion which I have moved needs to be determined before there can be another question put before the chamber. Penny Wong I am not sure; I may have misspoken or the manager may have misunderstood. I moved that the question on this motion be adjourned to a later hour. Bill Heffernan I move we go home for Christmas! Penny Wong Hear, hear! John Williams My advice is that, even if leave was granted, I could not entertain such a motion. I will put the question. The question is— Penny Wong Sorry; I ask for an explanation on your ruling. John Williams The motion put before the chair needs to be without amendment or debate; therefore, your motion is not in order. Penny Wong To clarify: I am seeking leave to move that the question on this motion be adjourned to a later hour. John Williams Yes, and leave has been denied. Penny Wong And I am seeking, therefore, to move that so much of standing orders be suspended as would prevent me from moving that the question on this motion be adjourned to a later hour pursuant to contingent notice of motion. Mathias Cormann Mr Acting Deputy","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-4041","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2015-12-03/4"}
